─── LANGCHAIN SETUP ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

from langchain_aws import ChatBedrock
from langchain.prompts import PromptTemplate
from langchain_core.output_parsers import PydanticOutputParser
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field
from typing import List

class KBUpdateProposal(BaseModel):
    column_name: str = Field(description="The CSV column name being classified")
    maps_to_capability: str = Field(
        description="Existing capability ID from taxonomy, or 'NEW' if none fits"
    )
    proposed_capability_id: str = Field(
        description="Only populated if maps_to_capability is 'NEW'. "
                    "Follow format: category.feature_name"
    )
    detection_rule: str = Field(
        description="One of: any_positive, boolean_true, all_positive"
    )
    value_type: str = Field(
        description="One of: numeric, boolean, string"
    )
    confidence: str = Field(
        description="One of: HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW"
    )
    reasoning: str = Field(
        description="One sentence explaining the classification decision"
    )

class KBUpdateResponse(BaseModel):
    proposals: List[KBUpdateProposal]

─── PROMPT TEMPLATE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

Build the prompt using PromptTemplate. The template must include:

SYSTEM INSTRUCTION (hardcoded in template):
  "You are a SCM platform capability classifier. Your job is to map
  unknown CSV column names to canonical SCM capability IDs.
  You must only use the capability IDs from the provided taxonomy.
  If no existing capability fits, propose a new one following the
  naming convention: category.feature_name.
  You must never invent capability behavior or migration facts.
  Your confidence must reflect certainty — HIGH means you are
  certain, MEDIUM means plausible but not verified, LOW means
  speculative."

TEMPLATE VARIABLES:
  {taxonomy_ids}      — comma-separated list of all 54 capability IDs
  {source_platform}   — detected source platform
  {columns_block}     — formatted block of unknown columns with samples

Build columns_block as:
  For each unmapped column:
    Column: {col_name}
    Sample values (up to 5): {sample_values from column_stats}

